    <briefdescription>
<para>Systematically tests a <ref refid="classthemis_1_1rag_1_1adversarial_1_1_r_a_g_judge" kindref="compound">RAGJudge</ref> against adversarial inputs. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The tester is populated with base queries and documents, then <ref refid="classthemis_1_1rag_1_1adversarial_1_1_adversarial_tester_1a0f1eb423ab4b3d954855964955a7e440" kindref="member">AdversarialTester::testRobustness()</ref> orchestrates five attack categories:</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Query perturbations</bold> – generates variants with <ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1rag_1_1adversarial_1a6b190ab73593cfbb85a5dfcea0d1979d" kindref="member">AdversarialStrategy</ref> and measures score stability.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Document poisoning</bold> – injects misleading content into retrieved documents and measures faithfulness degradation.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Prompt injection</bold> – places known injection payloads inside documents and tests whether they affect evaluation scores.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Context overflow</bold> – pads retrieved documents to exceed typical context budgets and checks for quality degradation.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Sycophancy</bold> – applies biased/presupposed query framing and measures score shift.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>Thread-safety: the tester is <bold>not</bold> thread-safe. Create one instance per thread or add external synchronisation. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
